---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: eprfs-meta-domain-neutrality
purpose: >
  Keeps the publishable metadata resolver/evaluator domain-neutral. This crate defines policy
  ontology, resolution, ValidatorProvider, typed requests, and typed outcomes; concrete Elohim
  repository policies live outside it and arrive through the provider boundary.
rules:
  - id: eprfs-meta-domain-neutrality
    policy: eprfs-meta-domain-neutrality@2
---

# `eprfs-meta` — interfaces, not policy instances

The crate may know that a policy references a validator and may ask a host to evaluate that
reference. It must not know what any concrete validator means. Reach-time governance catches a new
concrete validator identity through a background code review; the Rust architecture test proves the
invariant even outside an Elohim harness.
